        ":question/id": "5de59b3c-690a-5df4-9316-a0654c96dd17",
        ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 & 6 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{32}=0$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe entry in row $2$, column $2$ is $0$. Switching rows $3$ and $2$ therefore makes $a_{32}=0$.\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C &=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 & 6 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 & 6 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
