        ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{11}=0$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{11}=2+(2)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 11 & 22 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}.\n$$",
